Comments:
1. Evaluator: Kiana Setoodehnia, December 16, 2024.
2. The energies and spin-parities are from J. Chen et al., Nucl. Data Sheets 112, 2715 (2011). 
3. The spectroscopic factors are from P. M. Endt At. Data Nucl. Data Tables 19, 23 (1977).
4. The gamma-ray partial width for the sole resonance comes from that of the mirror state scaled for the 35K resonance energy. The mirror partial width is from J. 
   Chen et al., Nucl. Data Sheets 112, 2715 (2011).
5. The proton partial width is calculated from the spectroscopic factor provided by P. M. Endt At. Data Nucl. Data Tables 19, 23 (1977).
6. The experimental rate agrees with the TALYS rate at 10 GK within the uncertainties. Therefore, no high-temperature rate matching is needed.
